1
00:00:06,132 --> 00:00:08,476
Whiskers and the White Mountain.

2
00:00:19,407 --> 00:00:23,666
One frosty autumn morning, Pip came running with a postcard.

3
00:00:26,932 --> 00:00:29,626
Special delivery! All the way from the mountains!

4
00:00:29,826 --> 00:00:33,127
Mont Blanc! The White Mountain, the highest in all the Alps!

5
00:00:33,327 --> 00:00:37,084
They say from the top, you can watch the sun rise above the clouds.

6
00:00:37,284 --> 00:00:39,233
Clouds are just sky pillows.

7
00:00:39,433 --> 00:00:41,953
It says they serve hot cheese fondue up there.

8
00:00:45,219 --> 00:00:48,670
Hot... melty... cheese? Luna, pack the bags!

9
00:00:51,936 --> 00:00:55,759
So the two cats took the train, all the way to the Alps.

10
00:01:04,391 --> 00:01:06,785
Look, Whiskers! Real snowy mountains!

11
00:01:06,985 --> 00:01:10,077
They look like giant scoops of vanilla ice cream.

12
00:01:15,643 --> 00:01:19,459
At last, they reached Chamonix, at the foot of Mont Blanc.

13
00:01:22,726 --> 00:01:26,655
Then a cable car carried them up, up, up into the sky.

14
00:01:34,521 --> 00:01:37,165
Nobody look down. Especially me.

15
00:01:37,365 --> 00:01:40,278
Open your eyes, Whiskers! We're higher than the eagles!

16
00:01:44,311 --> 00:01:46,804
Ooh. Okay. That's actually... pretty.

17
00:01:55,436 --> 00:01:59,211
Cold! Cold! Cold! Why is the ground so cold?

18
00:01:59,411 --> 00:02:01,413
It's snow, silly! Come on, it's fun!

19
00:02:09,279 --> 00:02:12,922
I'm fine! I'm measuring how deep it is. On purpose.

20
00:02:16,954 --> 00:02:19,811
Bonjour! Are you lost? I am Margot, the marmot.

21
00:02:20,011 --> 00:02:22,374
We want to see the sunrise from the very top!

22
00:02:22,574 --> 00:02:25,595
Then hurry, my friends. Look! The clouds are coming.

23
00:02:34,227 --> 00:02:39,098
The wind howled, and the snow swirled, until nobody could see a thing.

24
00:02:39,298 --> 00:02:41,246
Luna? Luna! Where are you?

25
00:02:45,278 --> 00:02:48,572
I'm not scared. I'm just... very, very cold.

26
00:02:52,221 --> 00:02:54,378
Whiskers! Follow the sound of my bell!

27
00:03:03,393 --> 00:03:06,901
Woof! Easy now, little ones. Bruno is here.

28
00:03:07,101 --> 00:03:10,986
Climb on my back. My chalet is just over the ridge.

29
00:03:20,002 --> 00:03:24,384
In Bruno's chalet, a fire crackled, and cheese fondue bubbled.

30
00:03:24,584 --> 00:03:27,445
Is this a dream? A whole lake of cheese?

31
00:03:35,311 --> 00:03:37,846
Careful, Whiskers! I think the cheese is winning!

32
00:03:41,879 --> 00:03:44,788
I'm sorry, Whiskers. You got lost because of me.

33
00:03:44,988 --> 00:03:48,509
Hey. I heard your bell. I'd follow that bell anywhere.

34
00:03:48,709 --> 00:03:53,285
That is the first rule of the mountain. Nobody climbs alone.

35
00:04:04,217 --> 00:04:08,131
Before dawn, the friends climbed the last ridge, together.

36
00:04:12,930 --> 00:04:16,005
We made it! The top of Mont Blanc! The roof of Europe!

37
00:04:29,236 --> 00:04:31,405
Whiskers, look. We're above the clouds.

38
00:04:31,605 --> 00:04:33,644
It's a whole sea of sky pillows.

39
00:04:33,844 --> 00:04:36,347
Luna? Thank you for dragging me up here.

40
00:04:43,446 --> 00:04:46,476
And now, the fastest way down the mountain!

41
00:04:58,174 --> 00:05:00,469
Wheee! I am doing this on purpose!

42
00:05:05,651 --> 00:05:07,897
Au revoir, little cats! Come back soon!

43
00:05:16,529 --> 00:05:19,978
Back home, the first snow of winter began to fall.

44
00:05:20,178 --> 00:05:23,113
So? Did you touch the clouds? Did you eat the fondue?

45
00:05:23,313 --> 00:05:26,820
Better than that, Pip. We climbed a mountain. Together.

46
00:05:30,086 --> 00:05:33,537
Next time, though, I'm packing a lot more socks.

47
00:05:39,103 --> 00:05:44,068
Because even the highest mountain feels small, when you climb it with a friend.

